@namespace Showcase.Web.Client.Pages

@page "/palette-switcher/api"

<DemoPageHeader Title="Palette Switcher: API" ComponentName="FaPaletteSwitcher" DocSlug="palette-switcher" />

<ComponentSubNav BaseRoute="/palette-switcher" />

<p>Renders <code>.fa-palette-switcher</code>, reads/writes the current palette via <code>localStorage</code> and a plain vanilla-JS call (see <code>Blazor/CLAUDE.md</code>'s "no Blazor JS interop for client-only visual state" rule), and always reflects/updates the whole page's <code>data-fa-palette</code> attribute (a custom palette instead applies inline <code>--fa-*</code> properties — see the "How to use" tab).</p>

<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>CustomPalettes</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyList&lt;FaPalette&gt;?</code></td><td>Consumer-defined palettes appended after the twenty-eight built-ins. Each renders as its own dropdown option and applies its colors as inline <code>--fa-*</code> custom properties when selected, instead of a compiled CSS block. Default <code>null</code> — see the <a href="/palette-switcher">How to use</a> tab for an example.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
